  - governance
  - organisational learning
  - strategy execution
  - technology governance
abstract: >-
  Execution Intelligence is a Cralgo concept concerned with how informed judgement is
  carried from organisational intent into execution without losing the context,
  priorities and reasoning that made the original direction meaningful. The proposed
  contribution centres judgement continuity, uses execution drift as descriptive
  shorthand, and presents Context -> Judgement -> Priorities -> Structure -> Governance
  -> Execution -> Learning as a connected conceptual lens rather than a rigid method.
notes: >-
  Pre-publication citation metadata. The Zenodo DOI and final publication date will be
